- src/owner.js: the owner and NIP-OA attestation checks, adapted from
  src/features/agents/owner-attestation.ts at the revision named in its
  header comment.
- src/views.js: the New agent and Settings views follow
  src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx, built from the same buzz-app components.
- src/activity.js, src/history.js and src/transcript.js: the Activity tab follows
  src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx and src/bundled/goose/transcript.ts.
- src/react-host.js and src/save-footer.js: the same modules as in
  buzz-plugin-opencode, which hold no buzz-app code of their own.

The build also bundles buzz-app UI modules unchanged (the model picker,
the instructions field, the design system and its DeepSeek mark), from the
revision in scripts/build-plugin.mjs (BUZZ_APP_REV). The DeepSeek mark is
DeepSeek's, MIT-licensed, as buzz-app's NOTICE.md says.

The build (plugin/plugin.js, made on the user's computer) bundles the
noble-curves and noble-hashes libraries by Paul Miller, and React, React
DOM, Base UI, Floating UI, Motion and Tabler Icons for the views, and
react-markdown, remark-gfm (with the unified, micromark and mdast libraries
they use) and fzstd for the transcripts, each licensed under the MIT License
(@ungap/structured-clone: ISC; tslib: 0BSD). Their license notices stay in
the build.

DeepSeek Harness (dsh) is a separate program. This plugin does not include
it; it starts the copy that the user installed.
